  "dct_description_sm": [
    "The Global Flood Awareness System (GloFAS) is a component of the Copernicus Emergency Management Service providing global hydrological forecasts. This dataset contains daily raster GeoTIFFs derived from ECMWF ensemble streamflow predictions. Return period exceedance layers show the probability (%) that river discharge will exceed the 5-year or 20-year return period threshold at any point within the forecast horizon. Flood summary layers combine 2-, 5-, and 20-year exceedance probabilities into categorical flood alert information for different forecast windows (days 1-3, 4-10, 11-15). RapidFloodMapping and RapidImpactAssessment are experimental products providing estimated flood extent at 1 km resolution and potential impact on population and land use."
  ],
